WEBVTT

00:00.690 --> 00:03.180
So if we were to
ask ourselves, what

00:03.180 --> 00:08.860
is the value of our
function approaching--

00:08.860 --> 00:12.870
as we approach x equals 2 from
values less than x equals 2.

00:12.870 --> 00:15.330
So as you imagine, as
we approach x equals 2--

00:15.330 --> 00:20.860
So x equals 1, x equals 1.5,
x equals 1.9, x equals 1.999,

00:20.860 --> 00:23.520
x equals 1.99999999.

00:23.520 --> 00:25.540
What is f of x approaching?

00:25.540 --> 00:30.390
And we see that f of x
seems to be approaching

00:30.390 --> 00:33.780
this value right over here.

00:33.780 --> 00:35.860
It seems to be approaching 5.

00:35.860 --> 00:38.160
And so the way we
would denote that is

00:38.160 --> 00:45.510
the limit of f of x,
as x approaches 2--

00:45.510 --> 00:48.660
and we're going to specify the
direction-- as x approaches 2

00:48.660 --> 00:50.500
from the negative
direction-- we put

00:50.500 --> 00:53.462
the negative as a
superscript after the 2

00:53.462 --> 00:55.420
to denote the direction
that we're approaching.

00:55.420 --> 00:56.700
This is not a negative 2.

00:56.700 --> 00:59.510
We're approaching 2 from
the negative direction.

00:59.510 --> 01:01.960
We're approaching 2
from values less than 2.

01:01.960 --> 01:05.640
We're getting closer and closer
to 2, but from below-- 1.9,

01:05.640 --> 01:08.180
1.99, 1.99999 .

01:08.180 --> 01:10.850
As x gets closer and
closer from those values,

01:10.850 --> 01:12.590
what is f of x approaching?

01:12.590 --> 01:18.460
And we see here that
it is approaching 5.

01:18.460 --> 01:24.490
But what if we were asked the
natural other question-- What

01:24.490 --> 01:31.320
is the limit of f of
x as x approaches 2

01:31.320 --> 01:33.590
from values greater than 2?

01:33.590 --> 01:36.510
So this is a little superscript
positive right over here.

01:36.510 --> 01:38.484
So now we're going to
approach x equals 2,

01:38.484 --> 01:40.650
but we're going to approach
it from this direction--

01:40.650 --> 01:45.550
x equals 3, x equals 2.5, x
equals 2.1, x equals 2.01,

01:45.550 --> 01:47.194
x equals 2.0001.

01:47.194 --> 01:49.110
And we're going to get
closer and closer to 2,

01:49.110 --> 01:52.690
but we're coming from values
that are larger than 2.

01:52.690 --> 01:55.290
So here, when x equals
3, f of x is here.

01:55.290 --> 01:59.310
When x equals 2.5,
f of x is here.

01:59.310 --> 02:04.650
When x equals 2.01, f of x
looks like it's right over here.

02:04.650 --> 02:09.400
So in this situation, we're
getting closer and closer

02:09.400 --> 02:11.100
to f of x equaling 1.

02:11.100 --> 02:12.717
It never does quite equal that.

02:12.717 --> 02:14.675
It actually then just
has a jump discontinuity.

02:17.280 --> 02:21.680
This seems to be the limiting
value when we approach when

02:21.680 --> 02:23.820
we approach 2 from
values greater than 2.

02:23.820 --> 02:28.470
So this right over
here is equal to 1.

02:28.470 --> 02:30.660
And so when we think
about limits in general,

02:30.660 --> 02:33.880
the only way that a limit
at 2 will actually exist

02:33.880 --> 02:37.410
is if both of these
one-sided limits

02:37.410 --> 02:39.040
are actually the same thing.

02:39.040 --> 02:40.430
In this situation, they aren't.

02:40.430 --> 02:44.200
As we approach 2
from values below 2,

02:44.200 --> 02:46.400
the function seems
to be approaching 5.

02:46.400 --> 02:50.130
And as we approach 2
from values above 2,

02:50.130 --> 02:52.580
the function seems
to be approaching 1.

02:52.580 --> 02:56.150
So in this case, the limit--
let me write this down--

02:56.150 --> 03:01.140
the limit of f of
x, as x approaches 2

03:01.140 --> 03:03.260
from the negative
direction, does not

03:03.260 --> 03:09.850
equal the limit of f
of x, as x approaches 2

03:09.850 --> 03:11.280
from the positive direction.

03:11.280 --> 03:14.570
And since this is the case--
that they're not equal--

03:14.570 --> 03:16.880
the limit does not exist.

03:16.880 --> 03:19.650
The limit as x
approaches 2 in general

03:19.650 --> 03:24.930
of f of x-- so the limit of
f of x, as x approaches 2,

03:24.930 --> 03:28.310
does not exist.

03:28.310 --> 03:31.310
In order for it to have
existed, these two things

03:31.310 --> 03:34.030
would have had to have
been equal to each other.

03:34.030 --> 03:35.930
For example, if
someone were to say,

03:35.930 --> 03:44.760
what is the limit of f
of x as x approaches 4?

03:44.760 --> 03:50.100
Well, then we could think about
the two one-sided limits--

03:50.100 --> 03:53.340
the one-sided limit from
below and the one-sided limit

03:53.340 --> 03:54.230
from above.

03:54.230 --> 03:55.605
So we could say,
well, let's see.

03:55.605 --> 04:00.780
The limit of f of x, as x
approaches 4 from below-- so

04:00.780 --> 04:01.610
let me draw that.

04:01.610 --> 04:04.380
So what we care
about-- x equals 4.

04:04.380 --> 04:07.280
As x equals 4 from below--

04:07.280 --> 04:10.660
So when x equals 3,
we're here where f of 3

04:10.660 --> 04:15.850
is negative 2. f of 3.5
seems to be right over here.

04:15.850 --> 04:20.170
f of 3.9 seems to be right
over here. f of 3.999--

04:20.170 --> 04:24.360
we're getting closer and
closer to our function equaling

04:24.360 --> 04:26.050
negative 5.

04:26.050 --> 04:29.760
So the limit as we
approach 4 from below--

04:29.760 --> 04:31.640
this one-sided
limit from the left,

04:31.640 --> 04:36.320
we could say-- this is going
to be equal to negative 5.

04:36.320 --> 04:38.740
And if we were to ask
ourselves the limit of f

04:38.740 --> 04:42.470
of x, as x approaches
4 from the right,

04:42.470 --> 04:48.330
from values larger than
4, well, same exercise.

04:48.330 --> 04:51.060
f of 5 gets us here.

04:51.060 --> 04:53.600
f of 4.5 seems
right around here.

04:53.600 --> 04:57.950
f of 4.1 seems right
about here. f of 4.01

04:57.950 --> 04:59.000
seems right around here.

04:59.000 --> 05:00.499
And even f of 4 is
actually defined,

05:00.499 --> 05:02.370
but we're getting
closer and closer to it.

05:02.370 --> 05:05.670
And we see, once again,
we are approaching 5.

05:05.670 --> 05:08.590
Even if f of 4 was not
defined on either side,

05:08.590 --> 05:12.480
we would be
approaching negative 5.

05:12.480 --> 05:14.800
So this is also
approaching negative 5.

05:14.800 --> 05:17.720
And since the limit
from the left-hand side

05:17.720 --> 05:20.130
is equal to the limit
from the right-hand side,

05:20.130 --> 05:22.880
we can say-- so these
two things are equal.

05:22.880 --> 05:24.870
And because these
two things are equal,

05:24.870 --> 05:27.830
we know that the limit of
f of x, as x approaches 4,

05:27.830 --> 05:30.300
is equal to 5.

05:30.300 --> 05:33.690
Let's look at a
few more examples.

05:33.690 --> 05:41.920
So let's ask ourselves
the limit of f of x-- now,

05:41.920 --> 05:47.600
this is our new f of x depicted
here-- as x approaches 8.

05:47.600 --> 05:51.360
And let's approach
8 from the left.

05:51.360 --> 05:54.583
As x approaches 8 from
values less than 8.

05:54.583 --> 05:56.083
So what's this going
to be equal to?

05:56.083 --> 05:58.666
And I encourage you to pause the
video to try to figure it out

05:58.666 --> 05:59.220
yourself.

05:59.220 --> 06:01.210
So x is getting closer
and closer to 8.

06:01.210 --> 06:04.050
So if x is 7, f of 7 is here.

06:04.050 --> 06:07.840
If x is 7.5, f of 7.5 is here.

06:07.840 --> 06:09.920
So it looks like
our value of f of x

06:09.920 --> 06:14.740
is getting closer and
closer and closer to 3.

06:14.740 --> 06:17.430
So it looks like the limit
of f of x, as x approaches 8

06:17.430 --> 06:21.290
from the negative
side, is equal to 3.

06:21.290 --> 06:22.910
What about from
the positive side?

06:22.910 --> 06:26.500
What about the
limit of f of x as x

06:26.500 --> 06:28.790
approaches 8 from the
positive direction

06:28.790 --> 06:30.220
or from the right side?

06:30.220 --> 06:34.130
Well, here we see as x
is 9, this is our f of x.

06:34.130 --> 06:37.950
As x is 8.5, this
is our f of 8.5.

06:37.950 --> 06:43.960
It seems like we're
approaching f of x equaling 1.

06:43.960 --> 06:46.620
So notice, these two
limits are different.

06:46.620 --> 06:51.400
So the non-one-sided limit,
or the two-sided limit,

06:51.400 --> 06:55.677
does not exist at f of
x or as we approach 8.

06:55.677 --> 06:56.760
So let me write that down.

06:56.760 --> 07:01.330
The limit of f of x,
as x approaches 8--

07:01.330 --> 07:04.370
because these two things
are not the same value--

07:04.370 --> 07:05.875
this does not exist.

07:10.540 --> 07:11.870
Let's do one more example.

07:11.870 --> 07:14.120
And here they're actually
asking us a question.

07:14.120 --> 07:16.290
The function f is graphed below.

07:16.290 --> 07:20.420
What appears to be the value of
the one-sided limit, the limit

07:20.420 --> 07:26.900
of f of x-- this is f of x--
as x approaches negative 2

07:26.900 --> 07:28.120
from the negative direction?

07:28.120 --> 07:30.500
So this is the negative 2
from the negative direction.

07:30.500 --> 07:32.900
So we care what happens as
x approaches negative 2.

07:32.900 --> 07:35.542
We see f of x is actually
undefined right over there.

07:35.542 --> 07:37.250
But let's see what
happens as we approach

07:37.250 --> 07:39.166
from the negative
direction, or as we approach

07:39.166 --> 07:40.870
from values less
than negative 2,

07:40.870 --> 07:43.080
or as we approach from the left.

07:43.080 --> 07:46.450
As we approach from the
left, f of negative 4

07:46.450 --> 07:47.560
is right over here.

07:47.560 --> 07:50.330
So this is f of negative 4.

07:50.330 --> 07:52.900
f of negative 3 is
right over here.

07:55.880 --> 07:59.930
f of negative 2.5 seems
to be right over here.

07:59.930 --> 08:01.770
We seem to be getting
closer and closer

08:01.770 --> 08:04.840
to f of x being equal
to 4, at least visually.

08:04.840 --> 08:06.550
So I would say that
it looks-- at least,

08:06.550 --> 08:10.470
graphically-- the limit of
f of x, as x approaches 2

08:10.470 --> 08:14.670
from the negative
direction, is equal to 4.

08:14.670 --> 08:17.210
Now, if we also asked
ourselves the limit

08:17.210 --> 08:20.680
of f of x, as x
approaches negative 2

08:20.680 --> 08:24.267
from the positive direction,
we would get a similar result.

08:24.267 --> 08:25.850
Now, we're going to
approach from when

08:25.850 --> 08:29.470
x is 0, f of x seems
to be right over here.

08:29.470 --> 08:32.330
When x is 1, f of x
is right over here.

08:36.740 --> 08:39.350
When x is negative
1, f of x is there.

08:39.350 --> 08:43.809
When x is negative 1.9, f of
x seems to be right over here.

08:43.809 --> 08:47.400
So once again, we seem to be
getting closer and closer to 4.

08:47.400 --> 08:50.240
Because the left-handed limit
and the right-handed limit

08:50.240 --> 08:51.040
are the same value.

08:51.040 --> 08:54.180
Because both one-sided limits
are approaching the same thing,

08:54.180 --> 09:01.240
we can say that the limit
of f of x, as x approaches

09:01.240 --> 09:03.375
negative 2-- and this
is from both directions.

09:03.375 --> 09:06.090
Since from both directions, we
get the same limiting value,

09:06.090 --> 09:07.770
we can say that the
limit exists there.

09:07.770 --> 09:10.710
And it is equal to 4.
